<title>USA: NYCE cotton called to open steady to 0.10 lower.</title>
<headline>NYCE cotton called to open steady to 0.10 lower.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>NYCE cotton futures were called to open unchanged to 0.10 cent lower as of 1021 EDT, floor sources said.</p>
<p>They cited favorable weather in parts of the U.S. cotton belt.</p>
<p>&quot;It is raining in west Texas which is very good for the cotton,&quot; one Texas floor trader said. He noted that the cotton was blooming and setting fruit.</p>
<p>Friday, December cotton firmed 0.07 cent to end at 75.12 cents a lb.</p>
<p>((Doris Frankel, Chicago Commodity Desk, 312-983-7305))</p>
